{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"WAIVER_SCOPE_ATTRIBUTION","classStatement":"A review waiver must have one testable rule for which scope it closes.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC6, lines 77–83, closes any unpassed scope when a review waiver occurs after that scope’s latest pair, but attributes a waiver after a FAIL only to the workflow’s latest pair. R6, line 156, does not test a waiver following pairs from multiple scopes. The design’s D6 rule also identifies the latest paired round before the waiver.","failureScenario":"A workflow has an open slice review, then a feature-final review, then waives the review gate -> AC6 closes both scopes although the waiver is attributed to the latest pair’s scope, removing the earlier open scope from the median and potentially reporting the measure as met.","id":"F1","severity":"high"}],"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The proposed work targets #149’s metrics, CLI, desktop, and guide surfaces in one unmerged PR. The desktop fallback, avoidance of parallel-work files, and prohibition on touching a live remote metrics store match the human’s grant.","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"The spec cannot yet authorize implementation: its waiver rule can close the wrong review scopes and report a misleading rounds-to-PASS result."}